<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kamata Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1257 CE – 1498 CE (approx.) · capital Kamatapur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A kingdom of western Assam and northern Bengal that grew out of ancient Kamarupa and was destroyed by the Bengal Sultanate in 1498.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kamata emerged in the 13th century from the western remains of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kamarupa">Kamarupa</a> kingdom. Sandhya, a ruler based at Kamarupanagara, moved his capital west to Kamatapur after Turkic attacks around 1257, giving the kingdom its name. It then held the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karatoya-river">Karatoya</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> rivers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is documented about government under the early kings. In the 15th century the Khen dynasty ruled from Kamatapur, near modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cooch-behar-state">Cooch Behar</a>, where extensive earthen ramparts survive. Its last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nilambar">Nilambar</a>, controlled a large territory and defended it against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bengal-sultanate">Bengal Sultanate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaktism">Shakta</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a> and local cults dominated.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1498 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-husain-shah">Alauddin Husain Shah</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bengal-sultanate">Bengal Sultanate</a> captured Kamatapur by a ruse and ended Khen rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal's</a> hold proved short, and the region was soon taken by the Koch dynasty, whose kingdom later split into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cooch-behar-state">Koch Bihar</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/koch-hajo">Koch Hajo</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1257 CE – 1498 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.72%;width:4.80%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1257 CE – 1498 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kamatapur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sandhya, Nilambar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kamtapuri, Assamese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kamatapur, Khen dynasty, Kingdom of Kamata</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1378&amp;focus=kamata-kingdom" aria-label="Kamata Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6829 1354 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kamata Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7405 1478h0M7339 1518h0M7360 1467h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7149 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7149 1610h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=1378&amp;focus=kamata-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
